{
  "name": "Turn text into a voice-over or a music track saved to Google Drive (MartLLM)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Turn text into a voice-over or a music track, saved to Google Drive\n\nOpen the form, choose **Voice-over** or **Music** and type. A voice-over reads your text aloud. Music makes a track from your description (\"calm lo-fi beat with soft piano\"). The MP3 is saved to your Google Drive and the form shows its link and what it cost.\n\n### Set up (5 minutes)\n1. Get an API key at [martllm.com](https://martllm.com/go/n8n-voice-music) and add credit.\n2. Open **Make the voice-over** → Credential → Create new → **Header Auth**:\n   - Name: `Authorization`\n   - Value: `Bearer ` followed by your key\n   The other MartLLM steps use the same credential. If you already made it for another MartLLM or UberLLM template, pick that one.\n3. Open **Save to Google Drive**: connect Google Drive and pick a folder.\n4. Activate the workflow, open **Audio form** and copy its link. Share it with anyone on your team.\n\n### Price\nListed on 2026-11-25: a voice-over with Kokoro costs $0.0031 per started 1,000 characters of text. A music track with ACE-Step 1.5 costs $0.03, whatever its length (60 to 210 seconds). Prices move: [live prices](https://martllm.com/models).\n\n### What you pay\n- Each request costs what the seller that made it charged. No MartLLM fee on requests.\n- Anything that is not made costs nothing.\n- Adding credit by card costs 5.5% + $0.50. Credit does not expire while your account is open.\n",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "e8ecc368-7c46-5dc6-8821-48652587d475",
      "name": "Note: start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Change it here\n**Settings** holds the voice model and voice, the music model and track length in seconds, and the most one file may cost.\n\nEach model's page on [martllm.com/models](https://martllm.com/models) lists its voices and the track lengths it makes.",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "8491a018-f38d-5685-a08d-3ab7cd5f1bbf",
      "name": "Note: settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        400,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Waiting for the music\nA voice-over comes back in the same request. Music is a job: the workflow checks every 10 seconds and gives up after 10 minutes (the track still finishes and shows in your MartLLM dashboard under Activity). If something fails, the form stops with the reason the API gave, and nothing is charged.",
        "height": 170,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "33a6d20d-5439-5c40-94e4-d2c45cf17879",
      "name": "Note: waiting for music",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1080,
        500
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "formTitle": "Make a voice-over or a music track",
        "formDescription": "Choose what you want and type. The MP3 is saved to Google Drive and its link shows on this page. A voice-over takes a few seconds, music up to a few minutes.",
        "formFields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "fieldLabel": "What do you want?",
              "fieldType": "dropdown",
              "requiredField": true,
              "fieldOptions": {
                "values": [
                  {
                    "option": "Voice-over (reads my text aloud)"
                  },
                  {
                    "option": "Music (a track from my description)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "fieldLabel": "Text to read aloud, or the music you want",
              "fieldType": "textarea",
              "placeholder": "e.g. Welcome to our store. Free shipping this week only.   or   Calm lo-fi beat with soft piano, no vocals",
              "requiredField": true
            },
            {
              "fieldLabel": "File name",
              "placeholder": "optional, e.g. spring-sale-intro"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "buttonLabel": "Make my audio"
        }
      },
      "id": "815dcbf3-889d-5f49-aafd-454a59e3bab9",
      "name": "Audio form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        200
      ],
      "webhookId": "633e07f9-0a82-5e6c-aea1-c4c6612790aa"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Reads the form and names the file.\nconst f = $input.first().json;\nconst text = String(f['Text to read aloud, or the music you want'] || '').trim();\nif (!text) throw new Error('Write the text to read aloud, or describe the music.');\nconst music = String(f['What do you want?'] || '').startsWith('Music');\nconst stamp = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace(/[T:]/g, '-');\nconst name = String(f['File name'] || '').replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N} _-]+/gu, ' ').trim().slice(0, 80)\n  || (music ? 'music-' : 'voice-over-') + stamp;\nreturn [{ json: { text, music, file_name: name + '.mp3' } }];"
      },
